@startuml state-oai-record
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: an OAI record is live or deleted, never gone: deletion and withdrawal
'       from exposure both leave a tombstone that keeps its identifier, last
'       setSpecs and datestamp, which is what deletedRecord=persistent promises;
'       every transition sets the datestamp, a sync with an unchanged
'       fingerprint does not.
' Kind: UML state machine diagram, proposal (IP-033). Scope: one row of
'       oai_records (one per entry ever exposed). Omitted: storage details.
' Source: OAI-PMH 2.0 spec §2.5.1 (deletedRecord), §2.7.1 (datestamps)
'         (openarchives.org, read 2026-11-16).
' =============================================================================

title OAI record lifecycle: live, deleted, live again (proposal IP-033, 2026-11-16)

state "live" as live : header + metadata in oai_dc, marc21;\nlisted in ListRecords / ListIdentifiers;\nGetRecord returns it
state "deleted" as deleted : header status="deleted" only;\nidentifier, last setSpecs, datestamp kept;\nGetRecord returns the deleted header

[*] -[$accent()]down-> live : <b>sync: entry exposed</b>\n<b>(created in an opted-in catalog,</b>\n<b>or catalog opted in)</b>
live -[$accent()]left-> live : <b>sync: fingerprint changed</b>\n<b>/ datestamp = now</b>
live -down-> deleted : sync: entry deleted, moved to a\nnon-exposed catalog, catalog\nopted out or deleted\n/ datestamp = now
deleted -up-> live : sync: entry exposed again\n(same entry id)\n/ datestamp = now

note as N1
  **no transition:**
  sync with an unchanged fingerprint
  (a read, a popularity bump, an
  unrelated field) changes nothing
end note

legend bottom left
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | box | record state; its text: what a harvester gets |
  | arrow label | trigger / effect |
  | blue arrows | the normal life of a harvestable entry |
  | no final state | tombstones are kept forever (deletedRecord=persistent) |
endlegend

caption Identify declares deletedRecord=persistent and granularity YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ssZ. A row is created the first time its entry becomes\nharvestable and is never removed, so a harvester that saw a record always learns that it went away. Entries never exposed have no row.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · EvilFlowersCatalog · docs/diagrams/state-oai-record.puml
@enduml
